{"name":"Homestead","hex":"#ac8674","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Homestead","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A number of places in the United States:\nFormer name of Indian Wells, Kern County, California.\nA city in Miami-Dade County, Florida. \nA census-designated place in Iowa County, Iowa.\nA township in Otter Tail County, Minnesota.\nA township in Benzie County, Michigan.\nAn unincorporated community in Sugar Island Township, Chippewa County, Michigan.\nA village in Ray County, Missouri.\nA census-designated place in Catron County, New Mexico.\nAn unincorporated community in Blaine County, Oklahoma.\nAn unincorporated community in Baker County, Oregon.\nA neighbourhood in south-west Portland, Oregon.\nA borough in Allegheny County, Pennsylvania.\nA town in Florence County, Wisconsin.","Former name of Indian Wells, Kern County, California."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Homestead"}],"entries":[{"title":"Homestead (building)","blocks":[{"text":"A homestead is an isolated dwelling, especially a farmhouse, and adjacent outbuildings, typically on a large agricultural holding such as a ranch or station."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Abandoned_homestead_at_Nirimba%2C_Western_Australia%2C_August_2023_01.jpg/330px-Abandoned_homestead_at_Nirimba%2C_Western_Australia%2C_August_2023_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Homestead_(building)","wikidata":"Q5890494"},{"title":"Nguni homestead","blocks":[{"text":"A homestead in southern Africa is a cluster of several houses, typically occupied by a single extended family and often with an attached kraal. Such settlements are characteristic of Nguni-speaking peoples. A house within a homestead is known as an indlu, plural tindlu (Swati) or izindlu."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Angas_-_Zoeloe_vrouens_brou_bier.png/330px-Angas_-_Zoeloe_vrouens_brou_bier.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nguni_homestead","wikidata":"Q5890496"},{"title":"Homestead (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Homestead is a 2024 American post-apocalyptic Christian drama film directed by Ben Smallbone and written by Phillip Abraham, Leah Bateman and Jason Ross. Its stars Neal McDonough, Dawn Olivieri, Currie Graham, Susan Misner, Bailey Chase, Jesse Hutch, Kevin Lawson, Kearran Giovanni, Tyler Lofton, Emmanuel McCord, Olivia Sanabia, Grace Powell and Caden Dragomer. It is based on the book Black Autumn by Jeff Kirkham and Jason Ross."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/e5/Homestead_%28film%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Homestead_(film)","wikidata":"Q125424056"}],"images":[],"sounds":{},"pictures":[{"title":"Brown University 1792 engraving","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Brown_University_1792_engraving.jpg/500px-Brown_University_1792_engraving.jpg","ratio":1.5094170403587444,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Brown_University_1792_engraving.jpg","share":0.16625},{"title":"A brown building in the Jewish Quarter","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/A_brown_building_in_the_Jewish_Quarter.jpg/500px-A_brown_building_in_the_Jewish_Quarter.jpg","ratio":0.6667376037454777,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:A_brown_building_in_the_Jewish_Quarter.jpg","share":0.116875},{"title":"Vase with lamps, Brown and beige textures, Rostov-on-Don, Russia","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/Vase_with_lamps%2C_Brown_and_beige_textures%2C_Rostov-on-Don%2C_Russia.jpg/500px-Vase_with_lamps%2C_Brown_and_beige_textures%2C_Rostov-on-Don%2C_Russia.jpg","ratio":1.5049019607843137,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vase_with_lamp